      "id": "wire-protocol",
      "title": "Wire protocol and the socket server",
      "summary": "Unit tests drive the server over real socket pairs in both modes and with bad requests; the invoker's smoke test runs the real pair.",
      "subject": [
        {
          "path": "macos/rust/zazzled/src/.dev/contracts.json",
          "entityId": "wire-protocol"
        }
      ],
      "criteria": [
        "Requests round-trip through encode and decode, and oversize frames are refused.",
        "In descriptor mode output goes to the passed stdout, errors to the passed stderr, and the working directory comes from the descriptor.",
        "In relay mode the status and text come back on the socket.",
        "Bad, truncated, split and over-described requests do not stop the server.",
        "A peer of another uid is refused, and the socket is owner-only."
      ],
      "checks": [
